<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply rose $5.4 bln in Feb 17 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $5.4 bln in Feb 17 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $5.4 billion in the February 17 week to $3,867.5 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $17.0 billion to $5,015.8 billion. M-1 fell $6.4 billion to $1,076.7 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,862.6 billion versus $3,859.8 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
